# (e) REMOVED — was based on flawed star-import facade assumption. Inspection on
# 2026-06-24 showed all 205 src/X.py files in this list are FULL lazy-proxy
# facades ("""\nFacade ... lazy proxy\n""" + __getattr__ re-export), not
# simple `from clawcodex_ext.X import *` star-import facades. The src/X.py
# facade itself routes to clawcodex_ext.X, so the swap mechanism was
# redundant AND harmful — it pre-populated sys.modules with the ext module,
# which then caused Python to re-execute clawcodex_ext/X.py during the
# facade's own `import clawcodex_ext.X as _mod`, creating duplicate module
# instances with separate `_REGISTRY` (or similar singleton) state. The
# 205 modify patches that maintain the src/X.py facade content stay.
# See PATH_I_REVERT.md for the full post-mortem.

# (f) Facade migration — src/X.py is a sys.modules-swap facade pointing at
# clawcodex_ext/X.py, which holds the migrated fork-side implementation.
# Distinct from (d): here clawcodex_ext/X.py holds the FORK content
# (was previously src/X.py), not upstream 1:1. Suppresses the modify patch
# that would otherwise rewrite src/X.py from upstream full content to facade.
# Phase 4 P1 Step 2b — Tier A migration of 5 src/utils/ files. Run regenerate
# after adding/removing entries; series/b24b8cb_series will skip these files.
utils/git.py
utils/message_mappers.py
utils/messages.py
